WEBVTT

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.825
but from, again,
traditions and mentalities,

00:08:01.849 --> 00:08:05.796
or the interpretations of the Koran
that Muslims made in the Middle Ages.

00:08:06.224 --> 00:08:08.750
The Koran, for example,
doesn't condone stoning.

00:08:08.774 --> 00:08:10.750
There is no punishment for apostasy.

00:08:11.138 --> 00:08:14.196
There is no punishment
for personal sins like drinking.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:18.126
These things which make Islamic law,

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.954
the troubling aspects of Islamic law,

00:08:20.978 --> 00:08:24.074
were developed into later
interpretations of Islam.

00:08:24.098 --> 00:08:26.185
Which means that Muslims can, today,

00:08:26.209 --> 00:08:27.955
look at those things and say,

00:08:27.979 --> 00:08:32.282
"Well, the core of our religion
is here to stay with us.